---
// An opening paragraph with an illuminated initial: the first letter set large in
// Fraktur, rubric red, in a gilt-framed box. The letter stays part of the text, so
// screen readers and search read the word normally.
//
// Use it on English text only (lesson hooks are English): Fraktur capitals are
// decoration here, never German the reader must learn to read.
---

<p class="initial"><slot /></p>

<style>
  .initial::first-letter {
    float: left;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: calc(var(--text-base) * 3.3);
    line-height: 0.8;
    color: var(--color-rubric);
    background: var(--color-card);
    border: var(--border-gilt);
    padding: 0.12em 0.14em 0.06em;
    margin: 0.08em var(--space-3) 0 0;
  }
</style>
